Z||000000||FieroBUZZ||12-31-2001||09:38 PM||||I am considering a new computer. I'd like to try some sound/video editing and do some graphics work as well. The machine I have now is a Pentium III 600 Mghz and will go to the kids and for record keeping and word processing chores.<BR>I am considering the following basics:<BR>AMD Tbird 1.2 G processor<BR>512 RAM<BR>40 or 60G HD<BR>CD writer/rewriter<P>Any recommendations are welcome (remember I'm not rich) with what video/sound boards are good, etc.  <P>Gary<BR>I just drive 'em, I don't know what makes 'em work!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||avengador1||12-31-2001||10:05 PM||||Get the ATI all-in-wonder Radeon video card. I have the AGP card with 32 mb of DDR memory on board. The card will handle DVD, video in and out, and audio in and out. It also has a built in TV tuner and will turn your PC into a digital VRC. It also works real good with games. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Avendgador1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||isthiswhereiputausername?||12-31-2001||10:08 PM||||Check out <A HREF="http://www.ncix.com" TARGET=_blank>www.ncix.com</A>  (Canadian) and they will ship to you.  I find they have great prices and there is a page there that lets you configure your system and they will build it for you. <P>I definely agree  AMD CPU, burner? I suggest liteon or LG 24x burner (fast,cheap,buffer underrun protection, and supported by EVERY software program out there)<P>when you order your HD also, make sure its 7200RPM( dont try to save $20. by getting a 5400 rpm, not worth it....too slow..<P>||||reg||1
Z||000003||watts||12-31-2001||10:32 PM||||Your proposed system is about what I have.  If you're looking at doing digital video, make sure you end up with a mobo that has Firewire (IEEE-1394) on it, or get an add-on card for it.  USB is pretty much on everything, but it's super slow in comparison to Firewire.<P>More RAM the merrier!  Buy RAM now...  the price is going back up as we speak!  Get PC133 at a minimum - and you might as well buy 512meg sticks.  DDR-SDRAM is the best, but also a bit more pricey.  Steer away from RDRAM (Rambus).  I'm pretty sure it'll go the way of the dino's soon.<P>Don't bother buying the fastest CPU you can get - if you check the price/performance on say the top 4 AMD's, you'll see that you pay about twice as much for about 10% performance gain (I'm ball parking here).  The 1200 - 1400 range is fairly well priced.<P>Stick with a good brand of motherboard (I run an Abit KT7-Raid).  Check out tomshardware.com for all the latest reviews.<P>SCSI drives are really pricey, but the best for speed/transfer.  But if you're using Firewire for data transfer, it's not quite as important.  I'm using EIDE, and never drop frames.<P>The video card is a toughy.  Most of the cards out of Nvidia are good, and a lot of them support dual monitors.<P>Pick a nice case with about a 300+ watt power supply.<P>Pretty much any monitor with a Sony tube that's 17" + will cut it.<P>Anything I missed out?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Cooter||12-31-2001||11:03 PM||||Another question- How much are you going to spend?||||reg||1
Z||000005||FieroBUZZ||12-31-2001||11:12 PM||||Thanks for the info, guys.<BR>Cooter, I was trying to set a top of 2000.00 CDN.  I have a monitor, dvd/rom, keyboard, mouse etc already, and can steal the kids' burner if necessary.<BR>I am basically looking at the case and internals. Should I consider external hubs, etc rather than trying to stuff everything in  a case?<BR>Gary||||reg||1
